INT. SAFEHOUSE KITCHEN, SUBURBAN SPLIT-LEVEL - NIGHT

Drawn blinds. A table with a half-eaten pizza. Five people, each in a state of alertness that is nearly comic.

AGENT PHILOMENA OYELARAN-DUBOIS (40s, short gray hair, a pistol on the table) sits at the head. Beside her, AGENT GREGORY NAKAMURA-ACHEBE (30s, rolled sleeves, laptop), and across from them the WITNESS: HELGA BRZEZINSKI-MWANGI (50s, cardigan, a cup of tea going cold). In the doorway, two guards: OFFICER DIEGO FERREIRA-LINDQVIST (20s, earpiece) and OFFICER PATRICE ADELEKE-VANCE (30s, vest).

Philomena pours the witness more tea; Gregory glances at the laptop and mutters something; Diego shifts from foot to foot while Patrice peels back a corner of the blind and peers at the street; Helga takes the cup and stares at the swirl of leaves, and nobody speaks.

PHILOMENA
(together)
Helga, we need to talk about tomorrow.

HELGA ^
(together)
I'm not going to testify.

They stop. Gregory looks at Philomena. Philomena sets down the teapot.

PHILOMENA
You agreed.

HELGA
That was before.

GREGORY
Before what?

DIEGO
Before the car.

PATRICE
(from the window)
What car?

HELGA
The gray one. It's parked outside.

PATRICE
There's no gray car.

HELGA
It was there at six.

DIEGO
Patrice, check.

PATRICE
I'm checking.

PHILOMENA
Everyone be quiet.

They are. A floorboard creaks in the hall. Patrice lets the blind fall. Diego's hand drifts to his holster.
